  "query_preview": "..The second half of this week will be decidedly drier\nand less active for the panhandle of AK than the first half. A \nridge will build over the eastern Gulf and push north into SE AK, \nsomewhat breaking up cloud cover and suppressing precipitation \npotential starting Thursday. A strong shortwave over south central\nAK ought to provide enough support in its vicinity to keep some \nshowers in the forecast for Yakutat and the northern panhandle. \nAnother ridge builds in response to two troughs on either side of \nit in the Gulf, again quieting weather activity for most of the \nweekend. \n\nThere is uncertainty moving beyond the weekend as guidance is quite \nvaried in how it handles the second weekend ridge. The track and \ntiming of the next system depends on whether it can break down the \nridge, and when. As such, the confidence in the forecast for Monday \nand Tuesday next week is low, expressed with 30-50% PoPs for much of \nthe panhandle, as another wave might or might generate another round \nof precipitation.",
